---
const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Which versions of 3ds Max does it run on?',
    a: 'It is tested in 3ds Max 2024 and 2026. The script works with both Qt bindings found in those releases, PySide2 and PySide6. Other versions have not been tested yet; if you try one, an issue on GitHub with the result is welcome.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it replace the Scene Explorer?',
    a: 'No. It reads and writes the same layers through the regular 3ds Max layer manager, so both can stay open and both stay in sync. Nothing extra is stored in your scene file.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will it slow down a heavy scene?',
    a: 'Object rows are created only for the layers you open, at most 2,000 per layer (search finds the rest). Bursts of scene events are merged into one refresh, and nothing is refreshed while the panel is rolled up.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to objects when I delete a layer?',
    a: 'The panel asks first. Objects move to the default layer 0, nested layers move one level up, and the whole operation is one undo step.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I update or remove it?',
    a: 'To update, drop the new .mzp into 3ds Max: it replaces the old script and the toolbar button keeps working. To remove, delete layer_manager.py from the python folder inside your 3ds Max user scripts folder and remove the button from the toolbar.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is it really free?',
    a: 'Yes. MIT license, source on GitHub, no account, no network code.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="border-t border-line bg-card dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-card-dark">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-accent-deep uppercase dark:text-accent">FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Questions</h2>

    <div class="mt-10 divide-y divide-line border-y border-line dark:divide-line-dark dark:border-line-dark">
      {faq.map((item) => (
        <details class="group py-5">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-6 font-medium marker:hidden">
            {item.q}
            <span class="text-xl leading-none text-ink-muted transition group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-ink-muted-dark" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted text-pretty dark:text-ink-muted-dark">{item.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
  })),
})} />
